  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-Purpose Cash Response for Food Insecure Households Impacted by Drought</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following three consecutive poor rainy seasons in Ethiopia, with the rains of 2021 being particularly insufficient in Somali, Southern Nations, Nationalities, and People&apos;s Region (SNNP) and Oromia regions, some 8 million people are affected and in need of assistance. The food security situation in drought affected regions is expected to deteriorate further in the coming days, and this will have adverse effects on the lives and livelihoods of many pastoralists in the affected areas. The project will address urgent gaps and needs for the food insecure drought affected vulnerable populations in three regions of Ethiopia (Oromia, SNNP, and Somali). IOM, along with implementing partners, will target these food insecure populations through unconditional, unrestricted multi-purpose cash assistance in order to address basic household needs like food, livelihoods, shelter, water, sanitation and hygiene, as well as education and health.</narrative>
  </description>
